    "result_text": "The full suite is green. \n\nI implemented the disposable-domain blocklist as a dedicated pipeline step, keeping each piece of logic in its own single-responsibility unit and following the existing OfficeFloor conventions:\n\n1. **`ValidateEmailDomain`** \u2014 a new validation step that reads the shared `@Val OwnerFieldsDto`, extracts the domain, and throws when it matches the blocklist (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`). It sits right after `NormalizeOwnerEmail`, so it works on the already-syntax-validated, lower-cased address and skips the optional/blank case \u2014 no duplication of the email-syntax logic.\n\n2. **`DisposableEmailDomainException`** \u2014 a checked exception mirroring the existing `InvalidEmailException`.\n\n3. **`DisposableEmailDomainExceptionHandler`** + its escalation YAML \u2014 responds 400 with a `ProblemDetail` (reusing the shared `ProblemDetails.build` helper) carrying the rejected value.\n\n4. **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 wired the new `validateEmailDomain` step into the pipeline between `normalizeEmail` and `ensureUniqueIdentity`, under the same `transaction` governance as its neighbors.\n\nThe `errorRejectsDisposableDomain` acceptance test and the entire existing suite pass.",
